The new method builds its query from the selector's own `newQueryFactory()`, so the standard field list and the selector's CRUD/FLS settings still apply. `fflib_QueryFactory.setOrdering(...)` replaces the factory's orderings rather than adding to them. That swaps out the default `Name` ordering (which `newQueryFactory()` adds from `getOrderBy()`) for this one query only, so all other methods keep ordering by Name.

