   - This adds one extra query, and only when such cases exist.
   - Cases with neither an account nor a contact are left unchanged, as you asked.

3. **`without sharing`, on purpose.** Your integration user or the Email-to-Case user may not be able to see every account.
   - With sharing on, the rule would silently stop working for those users.
